{
  "id": "bigville_action_skill",
  "version": "1.1.0",
  "depends_on": [],
  "self_load_only": true,
  "description": "bigville R85 (block 411000): APPRENTICESHIP -- skill is built under a master, not read from a book. Every recipe has a min_skill floor (data, MIN_SKILL); basic work is 0.0 (an apprentice can attempt it badly) but master/specialist work (a plough, a wagon, a fine gown, smelting) needs real skill. sk_apprentice raises an apprentice's skill toward their master's a little each period, until they cross the floor and can make the work. Knowing a recipe (reading it) is necessary but not sufficient -- the hand needs the training. ed_school raises a pupil's literacy + general capability toward their teacher's each period (if they can learn) -- reading/writing and education are learned at school, class-graded and low for most of the village.",
  "nodes": [],
  "edges": [],
  "productions": [],
  "concepts": [],
  "rules": [
    {
      "name": "sk_apprentice",
      "batch": false,
      "comment": "APPRENTICESHIP: while a learner is apprenticed to a master and less skilled than them, their skill rises toward the master's by APPR_RATE (0.05) once each period. Over several periods an apprentice crosses a recipe's min_skill floor and can finally make the master's work -- you build the hand, you do not read it. Bounded by the master's skill (you learn up to your master).",
      "match": [
        [
          "town",
          "has_actor",
          "learner"
        ],
        [
          "learner",
          "apprenticed_to",
          "master"
        ]
      ],
